From 82d8219adf7ae61a9444c2e325897352322de1ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 09:49:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09914/11362] Substrate no-LLM recognition by rule; gate stops
 judging with a stale linter

exp6593 recorded an honest preregistered negative and was quarantined
DURATION_TOO_SHORT at 1.16s. Neither the linter nor the artifact was the cause.

ROOT CAUSE: the conductor runs as ONE long-lived --loop process. Its
fabrication-gate pass did a plain import of adversarial_verify, so it judged
artifacts with the module copy cached at first use. pid 4109305 started
2026-08-24 17:53:50; the linter had been edited 2026-08-25 08:31. exp6593 was
stamped by a 14h-stale linter under a rule its OWN commit (d5007390) had
already fixed. The dangerous direction is the other one: any fabrication check
added in those 14h was equally inert.

The band-aid in d5007390 was exp6593's agent appending its own substrate string
to NO_LLM_SUBSTRATE_ALIASES -- the guard admitting the artifact that needed
admitting. 41 of that tuple's 61 entries were the same no_llm shape, so the
list enumerated a concept instead of stating it.

CHANGES
- adversarial_verify: recognize a no-LLM substrate by name shape, after every
  allowlist, anchored so a _v2 suffix does not match. Same floor the allowlist
  already granted; no floor is lowered. Removed the self-served exp6593 alias
  so the rule is what carries it.
- adversarial_verify: SUBSTRATE_NO_LLM_BY_NAME (warn) keeps a self-declared
  match auditable, emitted before the duration guards so the 50 artifacts with
  no measured duration are not the ones it misses.
- research_conductor: reload adversarial_verify before stamping, with its own
  except so a partial file cannot skip the whole gate.

MEASURED over 18,833 artifacts, full verify_artifact on all 180 whose
classification changes: 6 lose a critical flag, 0 gain one. All 6 declare no
model, carry no model_specs, and were floored at 60s only by a vestigial GGUF
string. Independently reproduced by an adversarial reviewer.

NOT DONE, deliberately, both referred to the operator:
- exp6593 stays stamped. Clearing it means writing results/, which is evidence.
  200 of 565 stamped artifacts are stale the same way; re-verifying on read
  would un-quarantine all 200 at once.
- check_duration_vs_claim returns before applying any substrate floor when no
  compute marker is present, so a declared no-LLM artifact can record 0.0s and
  draw nothing. Predates this change, affects allowlisted substrates equally,
  102 artifacts sit in it. Closing it would newly quarantine all 102. A test
  pins the current behaviour so closing it fails loudly.

Spec: REQ-VERIFY-6593 + 5 SCENARIOs in openspec/capabilities/verification.
Mutation-proved: 9 mutations RED, restore GREEN, in a git worktree with the
module resolution verified by import.

